**who —** The Four Sages — the four wise men of the reborn world — Zebu, Tornel, Asina, and Kensu — who teach the hero the eight magics (Asina and Kensu are nods to Athena Asamiya and Sie Kensou of SNK's Psycho Soldier)

**what —** the four wise men of the reborn world — Zebu, Tornel, Asina, and Kensu — who teach the hero the eight magics (Asina and Kensu are nods to Athena Asamiya and Sie Kensou of SNK's Psycho Soldier)

**where —** XTL · Crystalis — SNK, NES 1990 (the US release of God Slayer, 1990)  Framework inputs: Crystalis; the four swords; the Tower; DYNA; the four sages; Mesia  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)

**why —** They are the keepers of the new order: the elders who hold the magic that replaced the lost science, parceling it out to the man who slept through its rise.

**how —** Crystallized from Crystalis (NES 1990) / God Slayer: Haruka Tenku no Sonata (1990).

**◌ the mythos —** They are the keepers of the new order: the elders who hold the magic that replaced the lost science, parceling it out to the man who slept through its rise. a being of the reborn world, the four swords, and the climb to DYNA

